/* book Worked example: Q: A broadcast FM system uses 75 µs pre-emphasis and a 15 kHz audio band. Find the corner frequency, the boost at the corner and at 15 kHz, and the SNR improvement from the exact formula and from the large-W approximation.
   1. f1 = 1/(2π × 75 × 10⁻⁶) = 2122 Hz.
   2. At 2122 Hz: gain √(1 + 1) = 1.414 = 20 log 1.414 = 3.01 dB.
   3. At 15 kHz: W/f1 = 15 000/2122 = 7.069; gain √(1 + 7.069²) = 7.139 = 17.07 dB.
   4. Exact: I = 7.069³/[3(7.069 − arctan 7.069)] = 353.2/[3(7.069 − 1.430)] = 353.2/16.92 = 20.88 = 13.20 dB.
   5. Approximation: (1/3) × 7.069² = 16.65 = 12.22 dB, about 1 dB low.
   Answer: f1 = 2122 Hz; boost 3.01 dB at f1 and 17.07 dB at 15 kHz; improvement 20.88 (13.2 dB), against 16.65 (12.2 dB) from the approximation. */
