/* book Worked example 2: Q: A receiver is tuned to a 98.3 MHz stereo station with Δf = 75 kHz. Find the local oscillator frequency (high-side) and the image frequency, the Carson bandwidth in mono and in stereo, and the stereo separation if the recovered 38 kHz has a 10° phase error.
   1. fLO = 98.3 + 10.7 = 109.0 MHz.
   2. Image = fLO + 10.7 = 119.7 MHz, outside 88–108 MHz.
   3. Mono: BT = 2(75 + 15) = 180 kHz. Stereo: BT = 2(75 + 53) = 256 kHz.
   4. cos 10° = 0.9848, so separation = 20 log(1.9848/0.0152) = 20 log 130.6 = 42.3 dB.
   Answer: fLO = 109.0 MHz, image 119.7 MHz; Carson 180 kHz mono and 256 kHz stereo; separation 42.3 dB. */
